{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pulls/1039","id":4866655527,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT_DsgM8AAAABIhNFJw","html_url":"https://github.com/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pull/1039","diff_url":"https://github.com/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pull/1039.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pull/1039.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/issues/1039","number":1039,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"test: prove Windows receipt-store pin identity and no redirection (WI-1083)","user":{"login":"xinglun","id":7902093,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDIwOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7902093?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun","html_url":"https://github.com/xinglun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Scope and entry\n\nIndependent ordinary `WI-1083-windows-receipt-store-pin-proof` at fetched main `00461714bd43d3f6c42ede66491e01d22d475604`.\n\nContract: `sha256:5b1c79efe1d3ade77cb13b75b238c1b46e68504bbfd8ce9cd00cb588edf49a5a`.\n\nOnly two test surfaces change:\n- `crates/cockpit-repository/tests/receipt_store.rs`\n- `crates/cockpit-repository/src/evidence_store.rs` test-only modules and a `cfg(all(test, windows))` call immediately after opening index.lock and before lock.lock.\n\nNon-test source bytes are identical after removing the cfg(test) additions. Public API, dependencies and workflow are unchanged. WI-1081/WI-1082 histories and resources are separate.\n\n## Proof\n\n- Move the Windows timing-sensitive scenario into a private library unit test. A per-worker thread-local one-shot ready/resume event carries the real opened directory/receipts/lock identities and paths. It means handles are open, not that the lock was acquired. The original persist implementation runs without copied write logic.\n- Drop the fixture lock File and short-lived identity probes before attempting rename while the worker remains paused, so the fixture cannot manufacture refusal with extra no-delete directory handles.\n- Both refusal and success paths preserve original directory identity, exact two-receipt bytes/objects/index mappings, public readback and no redirection. Original sentinel/no replacement index/restore checks remain. Same-path rename must succeed after all handles are released; only after every proof may errno5/32 be accepted.\n- Existing CI --lib runs a dedicated one-case native unit subprocess with an exact filter. The parent checks actual count 1 and success; native child command, phase identities, count and safety outcome are printed. No Linux cfg exclusion/zero tests is Windows acceptance.\n- The integration target additionally exercises the non-test public library: two-node persistence, complete index/readback and same-directory identity rename/restore after handle release. All other original integration scenarios remain byte-identical.\n\n## Evidence and current validation\n\nHistorical native RED remains immutable: WI-1081 head `00e89d21d6a00d09819f8353ae0a1391b954f171`, CI `38649495827`, job `116146092900`, receipt_store.rs:322 actual errno5 expected32. Decoded official job-log UTF-8 SHA-256: `8f7465da591db5cb5bc421e4ce3a7f6d72e47d1537d519303ec629f0f1f0ce8c`.\n\n- Deterministic numeric Win32 assertion-model RED at `37aeed15e4164b94c9d18667a25fa06e3b573a70`: actual 1 test selected, fails Some(5). This Linux model is not a native Windows claim.\n- Initial relocation hit the critical per-file test_weakening gate. No override/verification bypass was used. Meaningful non-test integration coverage was restored; fresh Runtime preflight then passed. All rejected admission evidence is retained.\n- Model GREEN: 1/1. Related Linux receipt_store integration: 12/12.\n- Full declared workspace/all-targets formal verification: pending.\n- Native Windows exact-case and related integration acceptance: pending CI.\n\nRaw commands, outputs and receipts: `.ai/evidence/WI-1083-windows-receipt-store-pin-proof.20261015/`.\n\nIsolated target, one Cargo build job, writable HOME/TMPDIR, host cap 900 seconds. This PR stays draft for Raydot source/evidence review. No WI-1083 merge, deletion or human close is authorized here.\n\n\n## Current full formal verification checkpoint (2026-10-15)\n\nEarlier pending/failure statements are retained history. Final admitted full `cargo test --workspace --all-targets` verification succeeded on exact source head `82521f19546b6d2c5504f71fbb71c03de551a9d3`: **13/13 nodes actually spawned, 0 reuse, all exit 0, no timeouts or spawn failures**. Host elapsed **731.8994 seconds < 900**; Runtime elapsed 727096 ms.\n\n- Receipt/checkpoint publication head: `c0fde42d263f8ce7486fe34711ea528d4b8b3d37`; only `.ai` evidence/governance changes since reviewed source `0ebf67b65a8663b1f631cbfd75147dd629648d99`. All crate source blobs are unchanged. Remote canonical receipt and full audit bytes were read back and matched local.\n- Contract `sha256:5b1c79efe1d3ade77cb13b75b238c1b46e68504bbfd8ce9cd00cb588edf49a5a`; snapshot `sha256:d5fc0425dd6b2f8b32ccc3a9bd7a75e9e319d48353e2b2b0b8a925987d05405f`; Runtime `sha256:5cca63a1b051da37b325b7d123842b6a4f7302f25cd235c0d22c12450c6b264e`.\n- Receipt digest `sha256:7fcad9ed79680b06bb864216ed1a3cc9aa0771c2301c7ae9c73452780fd5bce7`; canonical raw SHA-256 `239a5363abb47ee4bca32e1118dd459381e7be19bd4bf6a50a3d99bccead0049`. Full 13-member coverage and all execution records were checked. Repository stdout is bounded/truncated; its true flag is preserved.\n- Stable isolated target `/workspace/.tmp-wi1083-target-00461714-20261015`, TMPDIR `/tmp/wi1083-stable-tests-20261015`, writable dedicated HOME, one build job, one test thread. Only confirmed inactive regenerable WI-1082 and contaminated current-WI build caches were retired with byte/hash manifests; source, `.ai`, active worktrees, old WI-1081/WI-1078 caches and evidence were retained. All 13 package artifacts were freshly prepared without running tests or copying old binaries. Fresh CLI5/5 and original M1 1/1 prerequisites preceded the full run. One-second in-parent statvfs sampling reported minimum free bytes: `/tmp`2559180800, `/workspace`1667645440; these are sampled values, not a claim of exact continuous peaks.\n- All earlier formal failures, the stale-path ENOENT, ENOSPC, failed preparation, original Windows failure, targeted checks and canonical-provenance notes remain intact.\n- CI [38668285263](https://github.com/xinglun/ai-cockpit/actions/runs/38668285263) completed all4 jobs successfully on source head `82521f19` before this publication push; no record push canceled it. Official Windows logs prove exact native case1/1 (103 filtered), repository library104/104, receipt_store9/9, actual errno32 with both exact receipt/index readbacks and successful rename after all handles release. Quality40 passed +2 not_applicable. This source-head CI is distinct from the newly required publication-head CI.\n- Fresh post-push Runtime: checkpointed / green / verification verified, blockers `[]`; `user_visible_benefit_not_declared` remains explicit. **Draft retained; no finish, archive, human close, merge or WI-1083 resource cleanup executed.** Raydot reviews the fresh full receipt and publication-head checks next. Host display confirmation remains unknown.\n\nFull audit/logs: `.ai/evidence/WI-1083-windows-receipt-store-pin-proof.20261015/full-contract-stable-volumes/`; byte manifest `final-bundle-files.sha256.json`; source CI logs `ci-38668285263/`.\n","created_at":"2026-10-15T01:02:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T02:32:31Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8ed88c27c017d3833cc17c5f61f1bea0bc9845d3","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pulls/1039/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pulls/1039/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/issues/1039/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/statuses/c0fde42d263f8ce7486fe34711ea528d4b8b3d37","head":{"label":"xinglun:codex/wi1083-windows-receipt-store-pin-proof","ref":"codex/wi1083-windows-receipt-store-pin-proof","sha":"c0fde42d263f8ce7486fe34711ea528d4b8b3d37","user":{"login":"xinglun","id":7902093,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MDIwOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7902093?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun","html_url":"https://github.com/xinglun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xinglun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1341189248,"node_id":"R_kgDOT_DsgA",